process-loops.m's kinds spawned on the machine's GPU (docs/INPROGRESS.md, GPU
processes that run loops): the worker takes as its worker teams every team of
its module's kernel that no process uses, and runs its loops across them,
from arrays of one to a million elements; the echo, which runs no loops, runs
beside it in the worker's team.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-loops.m -o %t2
RUN: %gpu-env %t2 gpu | FileCheck %S/process-loops.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace

Without -fopenmp the directives are comments: the worker takes no teams and
runs its loops itself, one iteration after another.
RUN: merkc -O2 -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-loops.m -o %t.sequential
RUN: %gpu-env %t.sequential gpu | FileCheck %S/process-loops.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace

A second worker finds no team free of processes, which is an error at its
spawn rather than a process that waits for teams.
RUN: not %gpu-env %t2 gpu-second 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SECOND
SECOND: Software Error: process.spawn: GPU 0 has no team for the loops of the process kind worker: the module process_loops's kernel there has {{[1-9][0-9]*}} teams, and none is free of processes, which a kind that runs loops across teams takes as its workers

What the loops' bodies made goes with the worker's arena when it ends.
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_CHECK_MESSAGES=1 MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 %t2 gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FREED
FREED: Mercury runtime: 0 messages are neither read nor freed
FREED-NEXT: Mercury runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 0 rings are allocated
